Unix utility 'rmdir'

The Unix utility 'rmdir' removes an empty directory at a given path, absolute or relative to
the current directory, on the mounted volume. A directory still holding entries other than
'.' and '..' is not removed, and neither is one protected by 'protect' when the user asking
is not root.

USAGE:

rmdir <path>

Example of use:

rmdir /usr/local

It removes the directory local from /usr, if nothing is left inside it.

For more information, enter 'rmdir ?' or 'rmdir --help'.

HISTORY

This command appeared in the Hexagonix Mineru development branch (2026).

